Z||000006||Doni Hagan||11-19-2001||11:37 PM||||You guys are gonna love this... I saw at least 3 complete Northstar engines in cars at my favorite Chicago-area yards. The most I've seen charged for ANY engine is $350.00.. You gotta pull it yourself, of course although one place charges $50 to help you.. I got a $80.00 quote from one place for a 2.8 short block w/75K on it. <P>When I get around to doing my engine swap, I don't plan on spending more than $750-850 for everything. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||DR650SE||11-19-2001||11:40 PM||||Dani let me know how you spend so little.  I'm cheap, also what engine?||||reg||1
Z||000008||86 FIERO GT||11-20-2001||11:48 AM||||I got mine out of a car that went in a ditch and it compressed water in the #8 cylinder, very easy to fix, got it real cheap too.  Acouple weeks ago I could have got two more, they were mixin oil and water, no biggie just change a head gasket or intake gasket and clean the engine.  It costs 7 grand for a in the crate N* from cadillac.  If you find a 2.8 S10 and you can get the 700R4, it can bolt up to the N* too.<P>------------------<BR>If I can't beat the Civic next to me, Ill be polite and flip him off as he passes me.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Doni Hagan||11-20-2001||06:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DR650SE:<BR>[B]Dani let me know how you spend so little. [B] <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I go "yard hopping" like some people window shop. When I'm not in the studio, I'm in wrecking yards. Even when I tour. In most of them, Fieros go pretty much ignored so I leave business cards with the yard owners and get first crack at them when fresh ones come in. Example...Last week I bought a near-perfect pair of grey speaker seats (w/wiring harness) for $20.00! No bolster rips, burn holes or any damage I could see...just dirt. <P>Sevilles and El-dogs are not plentiful in yards but they're out there. I've got an STS with the N* so occasionally I'm looking for Caddy parts. <P>||||reg||1
